      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "> he will be able to re-download own (future proofed enabled/disabled) uploaded content from vrchat.\n\nOne issue I see with the future proofing option uploading uncompiled file is storage space. Unity will happily load a PSD (photoshop) file as a texture. So I've seen a PSD over a hundred megabytes used to provide a texture of about 5mb after texture compression. I think the future proofing idea is nice, but the amount of work required to grab the right stuff and keep workable is too much. Makes more sense to tell people to backup thier own files.\n\nIf people back up thier files they'll have them even if VRChat has trouble.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
