      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "if that's a problem?\n\nYou can use many free, paid or online tools that can multi-convert photos to other file formats at once.\n\nand if the user really care about retrieval of lost world, he will be ready to do a hard work to make it original as it was before, and on the end of the day his work will be payed off.\n\nas for the backing up unity projects, assets and other files matter, you simply can't predict when your HDD will die. and even if you backup your data to another drive, that another drive might also fail. i will just say 2 of many that can cause HDD to die:\n\nPSU failure\n\nOVERCLOCKING\n\nBut if you buy more HDD's to back up already backedup data that is already stored from many drives, that will be too much and it's very complex and not so cheap way to resolve this problem.\n\nand even if you backup to a cloud drive storage, it's very unreliable because even if it has encryption protection, it doesn't mean that your data will be 100% secure. and not to mention many cloud storage are limited, or they will clear stored data periodically. so to avoid this you have to pay for persistent data storage and eliminate other complications which is not ideal for some people who only want a free cloud storage services.\n\nso all in all i think that this future will not be so complicated to implement in vrchat's website or via vrchat ticket support.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
